module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.absorbing_fallback

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data absorbing_fallback: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "absorbing_fallback" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "absorbing fallback (a failure arm that widens — rerun everything, scan all keys, always run — instead of refusing; ⊤-as-answer conflated with ⊤-as-ignorance; the deficit's frequency zeroed by construction, the corpus-denominated cost breaking the budget later)",
    "UPSTREAM INSTANCE, 2026-09-07, and it governed this fleet's serving behaviour for weeks. vLLM's `EngineArgs.get_batch_defaults` probes the device for its memory and wraps the probe in a bare `except Exception: device_memory = 0`, commented 'This is only used to set default_max_num_batched_tokens'. On a GB10 the memory is UNIFIED, `nvmlDeviceGetMemoryInfo` returns NVML_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, and the handler writes zero — so the `device_memory >= 70 * GiB` test fails and a 121.7 GiB machine takes the small-device branch, selecting max_num_batched_tokens 2048 for the OpenAI-server context. The CUDA runtime reports the pool correctly (130,663,231,488 bytes); only the NVML path refuses. ",
    "WHAT MAKES IT THIS CLASS RATHER THAN AN ORDINARY BUG: nothing failed, nothing was counted, and the substituted value is PLAUSIBLE. 2048 is a real default that a real small device would legitimately receive, so the resulting configuration is indistinguishable by inspection from a deliberate one — which is why three separate analyses reasoned about the budget without anyone suspecting how it had been chosen. The comment is the author explaining why the absorption was judged harmless, and the judgement was made about the ASSIGNMENT rather than about the decision the value goes on to govern. ",
    "THE MEASURED COST, so the class carries a price and not only a mechanism: a 1,048,576-token-context model served on a 2048-token prefill budget. Because chunked prefill runs as a mixed batch, a co-tenant decoder receives one token per chunk, so its inter-token latency IS the step duration — measured at 30.1ms alone against 2168.2ms beside a cold prefill, a ~72x degradation, which is what users experienced as ~0.4 tokens per second. The value turns out to be defensible for the interactive objective among the arms that were measured, which is luck rather than design: nobody chose it, and it moves the moment the probe, the driver or the hardware changes. Rows at extdeps.vllm.batch_defaults and gunbc.spark.prefill_batch_sweep. ",
    "THE REMEDY THIS INSTANCE ADDS IS A CONSTRUCTOR RULE, not a review habit: a capability probe that can refuse must return a variant whose refusal arm CARRIES NO VALUE OF THE ANSWER'S TYPE, so `device_memory = 0` has no way to be written. extdeps.nvidia.management_library models the query that way — an unsupported query yields an arm with no byte count at all — which makes the absorbed substitution unwritable rather than discouraged (DESIGN section 4b(4)). The review tell is a `try` around an observation whose `except` assigns a plausible literal to the variable the observation was for. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
